\ A sleeping task is woken by a timer, which is outside the scheduler, so the pool is not
\ deadlocked while it sleeps. The body sits on a channel whose only sender is that task, which
\ on its own is the deadlock shape. The sleep outlasts the default five-second threshold, so
\ without the timer exclusion this run would report and exit 124 before the value arrives.

use "testing" ;
use "time" ;

[
  out: 1 <buffered-channel> ;
  [ 6000 milliseconds sleep 42 out send ] spawn drop
  out receive 42 "a sleeper suppresses the deadlock verdict" assert=
] task-scope
